Notebook[{

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["Causal Infrageometry", "GuideTitle",
 CellID->942062912,ExpressionUUID->"a3a3c038-ca24-47b7-9945-83f1c1312fe3"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Causal infrageometry studies the causal structure of a finite directed \
acyclic graph the way Euclidean infrageometry studies the metric structure of \
an undirected one. Events are vertices and the causal order is reachability; \
the objects are the causal future and past of an event, the causal diamond \
between two events, the worldlines between them (all longest chains at once, \
the timelike geodesics), the observers (all saturated chains), and the light \
cones, whose members are the light rays: the chains ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["[",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["v", "TI"], ",", 
    StyleBox["e", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox["]",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "cd772e26-bfa5-476c-ae6a-c000df59f42a"],
 " that admit no second route. Every object is an inert head that takes no \
graph. ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"InfraMeasurement", "[", 
   RowBox[{"g", ",", " ", "obj", ",", " ", "property"}], "]"}]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3c1dbde7-a6fe-407c-8e04-3d344d3a3bda"],
 " of InfraGeometry reads it on a causal graph, a named ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"RandomInfra", "..."}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "13833d5f-29ec-4a8f-92b7-fca3412f52af"],
 " sampler draws its members, an ",
 Cell["Infra...Q", "InlineCode",ExpressionUUID->
  "c47047bf-aa7b-407d-a6b8-cb0af4b217a4"],
 " predicate recognises one, and ",
 Cell[BoxData["InfraSubstrateHighlight"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "966cb862-21e4-4a4c-a957-b1bb37356b2e"],
 " draws it. The heads of two kinds follow the two InfraGeometry shapes: a \
cone, a diamond or a slice is a set, read by its vertex density; a worldline, \
an observer family or a light cone is a family of chains, read by the \
directed acyclic graph whose source-to-sink paths are exactly its members, so \
that cardinalities and densities come from one dynamic programme and never \
from enumeration."
}], "GuideAbstract",
 CellID->2001916300,ExpressionUUID->"ef0ab37b-2e0d-4399-8f7e-82603ccbe925"]
}, Open  ]],

